# What never needs to reach the builder.
#
# The line that matters is `data/documents`. That directory is the raw archive —
# 553 MB across four towns and growing — and without this file every `fly deploy`
# would upload all of it to a remote builder to produce an image that never
# reads a byte of it. The archive lives in a bucket precisely so that it does
# not travel with the code.
#
# `data/towncivic.db` is deliberately *not* excluded: that one is the point.

node_modules
.git
.github

# Development-only. `seed` is the only thing that reads fixtures, and a
# deployment that needs synthetic sample data has a bigger problem.
test
fixtures
docs
supabase
scripts

# The raw archive. Everything else under data/ is small; this is not.
data/documents

# SQLite's sidecar files describe transactions against a database that is about
# to be replaced by a baked copy. Shipping them would be shipping a lie.
data/*-wal
data/*-shm
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

# Never. `fly secrets` is how configuration reaches the machine.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
.DS_Store
coverage
